body:
I understand that the architecture behind should be modified to allow freed instances to remember its type, but until then and just to allow them to be removed from a dictionary, wouldn't it suffice to make the `Dictionary.erase` method not enforce the type constraints ONLY when the instance is null?

For example (I have no idea how Godot works under the hood, so bear with me):
```
void erase(instance: GodotObject) {
   if (instance != FREED_INSTANCE_TYPE && instance.type != dictionary_keys_type) {
      error("type doesn't match!");
      return;
   }

   // the erase logic...
}
```
